  "cause_chain": [
    {
      "source": "tongwenfeng.trime.yaml:1077-1123 and 642-655/731-742",
      "finding": "The standard keyboard assigns bh1/th1, bbs/tbs, bgn/tgn, benter/tenter and other custom per-key aliases. The Google+ and tantsing schemes omit them; fallback_colors only supplies candidate_text_color -> text_color."
    },
    {
      "source": "ColorTable.resolveRawSource",
      "finding": "A theme-only alias such as bh1 has neither a scheme value nor theme fallback nor built-in ColorKey fallback. Resolution correctly returns null; this is not a ColorTable chain-order error."
    },
    {
      "source": "Key.kt:99-116, 141-147, 156-161",
      "finding": "Unresolvable text alias throws through ColorManager and Key falls back to key_text_color. For the background, Key already uses nullable drawable ?: generic key_back_color."
    },
    {
      "source": "ColorManager.kt:169-194 on a047",
      "finding": "resolveDrawable sends unresolved bh1 to parseDrawable. Its failing parse is converted to Color.TRANSPARENT and wrapped in a non-null GradientDrawable. Key therefore never takes its generic background fallback."
    },
    {
      "source": "ColorKey.kt built-in fallback table",
      "finding": "keyboard_back_color falls back to border_color. In Google+ that is #dd4b39, also key_text_color -> candidate_text_color. In tantsing it is black, also the generic text color. Transparent keys expose exactly the same color as their letters."
    },
    {
      "source": "Current candidate ColorTable.parseValue and ColorManager.parseDrawable",
      "finding": "Shared classification maps an invalid string to Value.None, then null Drawable. A successfully parsed integer zero remains Value.Color(0), creates a GradientDrawable and preserves explicit transparency."
    }
  ],
